<h2>3. Alpha Decay: Why Signals Have a Shelf Life</h2>
<label class="sec-check" data-s="2"><input type="checkbox"/>Mark complete</label>

<p>Every edge in trading eventually gets copied, arbed away, or overtaken by faster competitors. This process is <strong>alpha decay</strong>: the signal weakens over time. The faster the signal, the shorter its half-life.</p>

